[error CommentBareTodo]: A bare TODO. Reference an issue or a URL, or do it.
     ╭──▶ test_resources/Rule/CommentBareTodo/bad-block-comment.hs@3:1-3:58
     │
   3 │ {- TODO a marker in a block comment is still a marker. -}
     • ┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     • ╰╸ A TODO needs an issue reference or a URL saying where the follow-up is tracked.
     •
     │ Note: A TODO nothing points at is a note nobody is holding. It reads like a plan, so the next reader assumes it is one, and it goes stale in place because nothing brings it back up. A reference makes it findable from wherever the work is actually tracked; doing it makes the note unnecessary. If it is neither tracked nor worth doing, the honest version is a comment that says what is missing and what would make it worth doing.
     │ Hint: To suppress, write this directly above line 4 of test_resources/Rule/CommentBareTodo/bad-block-comment.hs, and say why: -- [allow:CommentBareTodo] <reason>
─────╯
